@copilot Update this PR directly with one targeted simplification. In instrumentation/spymemcached-2.12/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/spymemcached/v2_12/MemcachedClientInstrumentation.java, narrow SyncBulkAdvice from every public getBulk overload to the canonical getBulk(Collection, Transcoder) overload. In spymemcached 2.12.0 and 2.12.3, all synchronous array/collection overloads delegate to that method immediately before it converts the keys to an iterator. Capture the synchronous bulk query once at that boundary instead of rebuilding it and opening nested context scopes in the delegating overloads. Bind the collection directly in the advice where that simplifies argument handling, reusing existing sanitization logic without introducing an unnecessary abstraction.

Preserve the bulk query snapshot and its cleanup, the asynchronous bulk completion/cancellation lifecycle, existing query text and operation names, iterator-key omission without consuming iterators, value redaction, the query-length limit, and descriptor-based CAS handling. Keep this change focused; do not rewrite unrelated advice or sanitizer logic. The existing synchronous/asynchronous bulk overload matrix and bulk cancellation coverage must continue to exercise the same behavior.

Apply the narrowest relevant Spotless formatter directly before behavioral validation and run the focused tests covering this change. Commit and push the change to this PR's existing head branch.

